 "intro_html": "Mame daifuku is a <a href=\"daifuku.html\">daifuku</a> with whole salted red peas (akaendo) folded into the mochi. Each bite goes salty, then sweet. The peas are soaked overnight and simmered with salt until very soft, since they firm up again as they cool. The mochi has less sugar than usual and a pinch of salt. Smooth koshian is the traditional filling; chunky <a href=\"anko.html\">anko</a> is fine too.",
