 "steps": [
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Rinse the <b>peas</b> and cover them with plenty of cold water and a <b>pinch of baking soda</b>, which softens the skins.</li><li>Soak <b>12 hours</b>. They should swell to about twice their size.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-1",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Soak the peas overnight",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Soak 12 hours with a pinch of baking soda; they double in size.",
      "src": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/1-how1.webp?v=c7c250ca2e"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/1.webp?v=35a131830d",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 1,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "12 h",
   "time_html": "<span>12 h</span>",
   "title": "Soak the peas overnight",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"30\">30 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Dried red peas (akaendo)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "a pinch",
     "name_html": "Baking soda"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Drain, cover with fresh water and boil for <b>5 minutes</b> to take off the bitterness. Drain and rinse.</li><li>Put them back with the <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"300\" data-s=\"0\">300 ml</span> water</b> and the <b>salt</b>, and simmer very gently, just enough to move the peas, for <b>30–40 minutes</b>.</li><li>Taste one: it should be soft right through and clearly salty. They firm up as they cool, so err on the soft side.</li><li>Let them cool in their liquid, then drain and pat dry.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "low",
    "label_html": "<span>low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Simmer the peas with salt",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Simmer so gently the peas barely move; taste one for softness and salt.",
      "src": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/2-how1.webp?v=cf4ae91bd7"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/2.webp?v=8897ddfda1",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~45 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~45 min</span>",
   "title": "Simmer the peas with salt",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"300\">300 ml</span>",
     "name_html": "Water, for the peas"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.5\">½ tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Salt"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Roll the anko into <b>6 balls of <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"25\" data-s=\"0\">25 g</span></b> and set them on a plate in the fridge.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Roll the anko",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Roll each ball between your palms.",
      "src": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/3-how1.webp?v=2fca2ce47c"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/3.webp?v=d1bb11f71c",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>5 min</span>",
   "title": "Roll the anko",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"150\">150 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Anko (red bean paste)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>In a heatproof glass bowl, stir the <b>shiratamako</b> and <b>sugar</b> together.</li><li>Add the <b>water</b> a little at a time, stirring and pressing out the lumps, until it's smooth and pours like thick cream.</li><li>Stir in a pinch of <b>salt</b>.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Mix the batter",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Add the water a little at a time and press out the lumps.",
      "src": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/4-how1.webp?v=c7f15f9273"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/4.webp?v=bc0180bf85",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 4,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>3 min</span>",
   "title": "Mix the batter",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"100\">100 g</span>",
     "name_html": "Shiratamako (glutinous rice flour)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"15\">15 g</span>",
     "name_html": "White sugar"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"120\">120 ml</span>",
     "name_html": "Water"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "a pinch",
     "name_html": "Salt, for the mochi"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Cover loosely with cling film. Microwave <b>1 minute</b> at 600–700 W, then stir hard with a wet spatula. The edges will have set first.</li><li>Another <b>1 minute</b>, stir again. It's now a sticky lump.</li><li>Another <b>20–30 seconds</b>, until the whole mass is <b>translucent</b>, glossy and stretchy, with no opaque white patches. Stir once more.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-5",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Microwave in three bursts",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "1 minute, then stir hard with a wet spatula: the edges set first.",
      "src": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/5-how1.webp?v=ee955a3d7a"
     },
     {
      "caption": "After the last burst it's translucent and stretchy all through.",
      "src": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/5-how2.webp?v=19377fce50"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/5.webp?v=b6e5581f4b",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 5,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~3 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3 min</span>",
   "title": "Microwave in three bursts",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Sift a thick layer of <b>potato starch</b> over a tray. Scrape the hot mochi onto it and let it cool for a minute or two.</li><li>With starchy hands, pat it out flat. Scatter <b>half the peas</b> over it, fold it in half and press it together.</li><li>Dust the top and cut it into <b>6 even pieces</b> with a dusted bench scraper. Keep the other half of the peas for wrapping.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-6",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Fold in the peas and divide",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Pat the mochi flat, scatter half the peas, fold it in half.",
      "src": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/6-how1.webp?v=d7eb7e2b8a"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/6.webp?v=dcccb1d329",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 6,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>5 min</span>",
   "title": "Fold in the peas and divide",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"3\">3 tbsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Potato starch (katakuriko)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Take one piece and stretch it into a disc about <b><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"len\" data-u=\"cm\" data-a=\"8\" data-s=\"0\">8 cm</span></b> across with starchy fingers. Make the edge a little thinner than the middle.</li><li>Press a few of the saved peas into the side with the fewest, so they end up spread evenly.</li><li>Set an anko ball in the middle.</li><li>Pull the edge up over the ball in four or five pleats and <b>pinch them together</b> on top. Twist off any extra.</li><li>Turn it over so the seam is underneath, and cup it in your palm to round it.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-7",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Wrap and pinch shut",
    "diagram": null,
    "diagram_title": "Diagram",
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Press a few saved peas into the bare side, then wrap the anko.",
      "src": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/7-how1.webp?v=5a3b2ee9eb"
     },
     {
      "caption": "Anko ball in the middle; pleat the edge up over it and pinch shut.",
      "src": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/7-how2.webp?v=ec12a5c859"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/mame-daifuku/7.webp?v=64e43b817a",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 7,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "10 min",
   "time_html": "<span>10 min</span>",
   "title": "Wrap and pinch shut",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Brush off the loose starch.</li><li>Serve the same day, at room temperature. Cut one in half with a wet knife to show the red peas dotted through the white mochi around the dark anko.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
   "id": "step-8",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Brush and serve",
    "diagram": null,
